SRC/eff_lp -- changes made for the OSK freeware collection  lpq.c    the job table's printer test passed strcmp() one CHARACTER of           the printer's name, queue->printer[n][0], where the name itself           belongs -- K&R C has no prototype to catch it.  strcmp then read           a string at the character's value as an address, low memory, so           whether a job was listed depended on what that memory held:           with zeros there every job was skipped and lpq said `No           Spooljobs' over a queue it had just counted.  The [0] is gone.           Found by the os9exec session, 2026-09-25.  The original is           lpq.c.ori.  lpsched.c  when a job queued with `lp -m' is done, lpsched looks up whom           to mail with getpwuid(queue->jobs[jo].user&&0xffff) -- a logical           AND, 1 for every user, so the mail went to user number 1.  It is           `&' now, as lp.c has it.  <errno.h> is included for the errno           it reads, which this SDK needs to compile it.  The original is           lpsched.c.ori.           THE SHIPPED BINARY IS NOT A REBUILD.  The archive's lpsched           carries a getpwuid that reads /dd/SYS/password; this SDK has           none, and a rebuild would link the USER shim, which names           whoever started the daemon.  So the shipped binary is the           archive's with that one expression changed in place --           tools/patch_lpsched.py, 2026-09-26.